<div class="wrap">
  <div class="quote-banner">
    <div class="qi">&#128274; <b>Prepared for {{ customer.first_name | default: 'you' }}</b> &middot; Quote {{ product.metafields.crm.quote_no | default: '#Q' }} &middot; private listing.</div>
    {%- if product.metafields.crm.expires_at -%}<div class="exp">Expires <b>{{ product.metafields.crm.expires_at | date: '%b %-d, %Y' }}</b></div>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
  <div class="pdp">
    {%- comment -%}
      Hero image, in priority order: the product's featured image (the publish worker attaches the
      door render as the first product image, so Shopify HOSTS it — reliable, always paints), then
      the CRM 4K render metafield URL (crm.render_4k, browser-fetched from Supabase — a fallback for
      products published before the render was hosted). NOTE crm.render_4k is a `url`-type metafield —
      read its `.value` (the metafield OBJECT renders empty inside url(), which blanks the viewer).
      The "4K render ready" badge shows whenever a render backs the viewer.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign render_url = product.metafields.crm.render_4k.value -%}
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      {%- assign hero_src = product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1600 -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign hero_src = render_url -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="pl-media">
      <div class="viewer" id="pl-viewer" {% if hero_src != blank %}style="background-image:url('{{ hero_src }}')"{% endif %}>
        <div class="hud">&#8635; &#10530; AR</div>
        {%- if hero_src != blank -%}<div class="rstate">&#9679; 4K render ready</div>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Front thumbnails: the door/drawer-front renders the pipeline attaches as product images
        (product.images — the door render leads, so it's also the hero above). Clicking one swaps the
        viewer background (progressive enhancement; the hero still shows with JS off). Only when the
        hero came from the metafield URL instead (no product images) do we add a standalone hero thumb.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign thumb_count = product.images | size -%}
      {%- if thumb_count > 0 or hero_src != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%} data-full carries the hi-res URL (attribute-escaped); the handler reads it —
          so a CDN URL's ?v=…&width=… can't break out of the inline JS string. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="pl-thumbs" onclick="if(event.target.dataset.full){document.getElementById('pl-viewer').style.backgroundImage=&quot;url('&quot;+event.target.dataset.full+&quot;')&quot;}">
          {%- if thumb_count == 0 and hero_src != blank -%}
            <button type="button" class="pl-thumb is-hero" data-full="{{ hero_src | escape }}" style="background-image:url({{ hero_src }})" aria-label="Show render"></button>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- for image in product.images -%}
            <button type="button" class="pl-thumb" data-full="{{ image | image_url: width: 1600 | escape }}" style="background-image:url({{ image | image_url: width: 240 }})" aria-label="{{ image.alt | default: 'Front detail' | escape }}"></button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {% form 'product', product, class: 'product-form' %}
    {%- assign pl_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first -%}
    <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ pl_variant.id }}">
    <div class="details">
      <span class="eyebrow">Your custom quote</span>
      <h1>{{ product.title }}</h1>
      <div class="price">{{ product.price | money }} &middot; made to order</div>

      <div class="opt"><label>Set by your quote</label>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          {%- for chip in product.metafields.crm.locked_options.value -%}
            <span class="locked">&#128274; {{ chip }}</span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="locked">&#128274; (locked options from the quote)</span>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        G-41: the "hybrid" editable-options block was removed. Every option on a private commission
        is locked by the quote; the buyer-editable-options flow (with live Cart Transform re-pricing)
        has no producing code yet, so rendering it shipped dead, non-functional controls. Restore this
        block together with crm.editable_options (publish-worker.ts) when the hybrid flow is real.
      {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The quote's design details — door/drawer style, materials, panel grain orientation,
        special notes — carried into the listing description by the publish pipeline. body_html
        is CRM-built + escaped (listing-payload.ts descriptionHtml), safe to render as-is.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if product.description != blank -%}
        <div class="spec-details rte">{{ product.description }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="hint">Every option here is set by your quote (&#128274;). Review the details and check out &mdash; your price is locked in.</div>
      {% render 'price-block' %}
    </div>
    {% endform %}
  </div>
</div>
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Private listing",
  "settings": [

  ]
}
{% endschema %}
